// The compensation showcase for REQ-AUTO-4.
//
// This flow is not a migration of anything: it is the fixture that exercises the
// abort policy `onFailure=compensate:<story>`, which no legacy flow could express.
// It reuses execution.flow's scenario names and steps so the two read together,
// and adds the one scenario the original never had — "cancel booking" — as the
// compensating story.
//
// The first migration of execution.flow folded this into that file, which cost it
// three of its original scenario names and added a scenario the original did not
// contain. Keeping the showcase here leaves execution.flow a faithful migration
// (P0-F2).

scenario (onFailure=compensate:cancel booking): book a slot
  Click the Book a slot link
  Click the location field
  Type "indra" into the location field
  Click the Indiranagar suggestion
  Click the next button
  Click the Book now button

scenario (onFailure=compensate:cancel booking): pay for the slot
  Click the booking result
  Click the Checkout link
  Type {data.card.number} into the card number field
  Select "08" in the expiry month select
  Select "2027" in the expiry year select
  Type {data.card.cvv} into the CVV field
  Click the pay button

// The compensating story. It runs with the failing flow's scope and then the
// flow stops (LLD §8.3), so a booking created before the failure is not left
// behind.
scenario (idempotent): cancel booking
  Click the Bookings link
  Click the cancel booking button

compose: book and pay
  book a slot
  pay for the slot

test: book and pay
